+/* Preferred video codec for yt-dlp's format selection. A preference, not a
+ * requirement: the selector asks for this codec at the requested height
+ * first and falls back to any codec, then to a progressive file, so a video
+ * that lacks it still plays. YouTube's H.264 ladder stops at 1080p; 1440p and
+ * above exist only as VP9 or AV1, which is what makes those two matter. The
+ * decoder that ends up running is GStreamer's choice (decodebin autoplugs by
+ * rank), see GStreamerPlayer::decoder_for(). */
